  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "The same failure as beta.3, one system further on. `NodeSyncSystem3D` writes a simulated position onto\na linked node only for entities tagged `SyncToNode3D`, and that tag is opt-in so a game can drive a\nlinked node itself. Leave it off by accident and the system matches nothing, moves no node, and says\nnothing: the simulation keeps running, so bodies walk, shoot and pick things up from positions nobody\ncan see, while every picture stays at the spawn point. From inside a first-person game that reads as\nbroken input — no walking, no turning, shots leaving from somewhere off to one side.\n\n### Added\n\n- `NodeSyncSystem3D.UnsyncedLinkedCount`: entities carrying a node and a position that this system is\n  not allowed to move. Zero in a working game; anything higher is a scene that will not animate no\n  matter how correct the simulation is. Computed only on updates that moved nothing, so a running game\n  never pays for it. The counterpart of `NetPredictionSystem.UnpredictableAvatarCount`.",
